## Cohesion Audit: Duke-Dennis.md

### Central Thesis

Duke Dennis is a Type 8 whose entire biography — the Army regret, the factory walkout, the sealed AMP circle, the hatred of "rizz," the name he never asked about — is one repeating pattern: refusing to live inside arrangements other people made for him.

### Thread Map

1. **Cold open / intro** — The factory walkout and the "rizz" refusal are framed as the same act ("Both walks are the same walk"), stating the thesis explicitly before any section begins.
2. **What is Duke Dennis's personality type?** — Formalizes the pattern as Type 8 using his own repeated words ("I don't like being told what to do," three times), briefly pressure-tests Type 3, defers the full counter-case to the Rabbit Hole.
3. **Why Duke Dennis calls the Army his biggest regret** — The biographical origin of the allergy: reception night, the "I don't want to be here" confession, and the paradox that he stayed anyway. Plants "Germany deserves its own section" for later payoff.
4. **How Duke Dennis built an empire on a borrowed email** — The escape route: YouTube discovered inside the contract, the first check that ended the factory, consistency doctrine, and the physique as the one self-governed territory.
5. **Why AMP will never add a seventh member** — The pattern applied to relationships: a sealed circle he controls, the one legal cost of standing in someone else's crowd (Union Square), and ranking-audits on behalf of excluded friends.
6. **Why Duke Dennis hates the word rizz** — The thesis's payoff: a label repeated daily becomes a schedule someone else wrote, explicitly linked back to the Army ("four years performing somebody else's script").
7. **Professor Dennis's syllabus** — The inversion: he teaches the exact meme economy that claimed him, with the Unit 3 contradiction explicitly cashed and Unit 4 named as the self-defense.
8. **What stress does to Duke Dennis** — Pays off the planted Germany promise; withdrawal-to-Five under pressure, then the doors opening (first interview, Dee shirt, growth-to-Two provider moves).
9. **The name he never asked about** — The close gathers every thread (Army, factory, Aspen, Unc) into the aunt's name: "a sound with no orders inside."

The map reads as a coherent outline top to bottom. Every section serves the thesis; removing any one of them would leave a hole in the argument.

